Alembic migrations for PARIVART.

    alembic upgrade head          # bring the configured database up to date
    alembic downgrade -1          # step back one revision
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."   # draft a revision from model changes
    alembic current               # what the database is stamped at

The database URL is read from app.core.config.settings (that is, from .env), not from
alembic.ini, so migrations always target the same database the API uses.

Introducing Alembic to an already-deployed database: stamp it at the baseline revision
that matches its current shape, then upgrade.

    alembic stamp 0001_baseline_schema
    alembic upgrade head
